{
  "_comment": [
    "Vehicle → platform rules. Authored Phase 3 (2026-09-20) under ADR-001 §5 Phase 3 and ADR-003. A wrong rule here is somebody's disassembled engine — every change goes on a branch, gets reviewed, and must pass  npm run validate-fitment.",
    "Rule shape: make + model + year_start..year_end + engine  →  platform. Every field is required and must not be blank. Years are plain numbers. 'platform' must exactly match a handle in fitment/platforms.json.",
    "The engine string is what resolves a platform when the same make/model/year has more than one — e.g. a 1999 GMC Sierra 1500 is sbc-gen1-vortec with the 5.7L Vortec and ls-gen3-early with the 4.8L or 5.3L. Spell each engine exactly the same way everywhere; these strings become the Engine dropdown.",
    "LS Gen III is split at 2003/2004 (head-bolt length change) per ADR-003 — a vehicle that spans the line gets two rules. The Small-Block Chevy platform covers the Vortec-head (8-bolt intake) engines only; earlier Gen I engines are deliberately not mapped.",
    "Deliberately NOT covered (they look similar and are not): 1992–1997 LT1/LT4 (Gen II, not Gen I); 2005+ LS2 Corvette/GTO/SSR, 2007 new-body Silverado/Sierra/Tahoe/Yukon/Avalanche/Escalade, Trailblazer/Envoy 5.3L (all Gen IV); Tacoma 2.4L 2RZ-FE (not a 3RZ).",
    "Scope note: launch coverage is the set of vehicles confirmed on 2026-09-20. Vehicles are added as they come up, one rule at a time, same review."
  ],
